the-history-of-the-work-2 : Part
the-history-of-the-work-2 = referring (cons "Avik, 2026-11-15 (02:22 UTC, 16 November), asking for a complete timeline of the repository:" (cons "" (cons "> ideally, this should be machine-generated/regenerable , but not bloated/redundant ie all internal relations preserved if that makes sense. how did organization move over time addition etc." (cons ">" (cons (quoted (cons "> actually " (cons "hyperactivity history" (cons " should enter history explorer in the product (eventually) . I would like to see how excellently we can do this inserting zero llm judgement at run-time. obviously, judiciousness/agency about depth/detail is essential i.e. we have entire papers, thousands of lines of code, showing the complete diff over time is inadmissible. the workflow system is part of it but that does not cover all action in the repo. this should be navigable, as CLI and web UI eventually." nil)))) (cons "" nil)))))) (cons "Avik, 2026-11-15 (02:22 UTC, 16 November), asking for a complete timeline of the work in the hyperactivity repository, the history of the work:" (cons "" (cons "> ideally, this should be machine-generated/regenerable , but not bloated/redundant ie all internal relations preserved if that makes sense. how did organization move over time addition etc." (cons ">" (cons (quoted (cons "> actually " (cons "hyperactivity history" (cons " should enter history explorer in the product (eventually) . I would like to see how excellently we can do this inserting zero llm judgement at run-time. obviously, judiciousness/agency about depth/detail is essential i.e. we have entire papers, thousands of lines of code, showing the complete diff over time is inadmissible. the workflow system is part of it but that does not cover all action in the repo. this should be navigable, as CLI and web UI eventually." nil)))) nil)))))
