the-history-of-the-work-3 = referring (cons "Then, on a first proposal that grouped the history into eras by top-level folders and by session:" (cons "" (cons "> deeply integrated perfectly fit to the intelligent design of hyperactivity. intelligent design is real and demonstrated precisely here. anything that is not the exact correct intelligent design is precisely incorrect." (cons "" nil)))) (cons "Avik, 2026-11-15, on a first proposal for the history of the work that grouped it into eras by top-level folders and by session:" (cons "" (cons "> deeply integrated perfectly fit to the intelligent design of hyperactivity. intelligent design is real and demonstrated precisely here. anything that is not the exact correct intelligent design is precisely incorrect." nil)))
the-history-of-the-work-4 : Part
the-history-of-the-work-4 = referring (cons "Then, on the first build (a second store, change objects, path-qualified names, folders and file" (cons "types as categories):" (cons "" (cons "> I said we’re moving off of git asap right. So is it wise to add a bunch of machinery?" (cons ">" (cons "> Near zero machinery. What did I say. Did I mention intelligent design? Do you know what that means? Are you actually even familiar w hyperactivity?" (cons "" nil))))))) (cons "Avik, 2026-11-15, on the first build of a history explorer for the work (a second store, change objects, path-qualified names, folders and file" (cons "types as categories):" (cons "" (cons "> I said we’re moving off of git asap right. So is it wise to add a bunch of machinery?" (cons ">" (cons "> Near zero machinery. What did I say. Did I mention intelligent design? Do you know what that means? Are you actually even familiar w hyperactivity?" nil))))))
the-history-of-the-work-5 : Part
the-history-of-the-work-5 = referring (cons "What follows (2026-11-15). An object is its content, so nothing is overwritten and the history is" (cons "already present: in the store, its log of names bound to keys over time; while git is the stand-in," (cons "git itself. A history explorer adds no structure and keeps nothing. It reads what is there when" (cons "asked, and reports only what the work declares: its nodes (type Node, and Ticket before it), the" (cons "leaves in progress and resolved, and the documents its code points to. Folders, file types and" (cons "sessions organize nothing. Its views are code of the language, evaluated by the machine over the work's" (cons "own values, as the task graph's views are." (cons "" nil)))))))) (cons "What follows from Avik's corrections for the history explorer (2026-11-15). An object is its content, so nothing is overwritten and the history is" (cons "already present: in the store, its log of names bound to keys over time; while git is the stand-in," (cons "git itself. A history explorer adds no structure and keeps nothing. It reads what is there when" (cons "asked, and reports only what the work declares: its nodes (type Node, and Ticket before it), the" (cons "leaves in progress and resolved, and the documents its code points to. Folders, file types and" (cons "sessions organize nothing. Its views are code of the language, evaluated by the machine over the work's" (cons "own values, as the task graph's views are." nil)))))))
